Short Description:
The Chinese Canadian National Council Toronto Chapter (CCNCTO) is an organization of Chinese Canadians in the City of Toronto that promotes equity, social justice, inclusive civic participation, and respect for diversity. Our team leads grassroots efforts to advocate for civil rights, promote positive race relations, and celebrate the rich history and culture of Chinese Canadians.

Our mandate is to:
1. Promote all rights of all individuals, in particular, those of Chinese Canadians and to encourage their full and equal participation in Canadian society; 
2. Create an environment in this country in which all rights of all individuals are fully recognized and protected;
3. Promote understanding and cooperation between Chinese Canadians and all other ethnic, cultural and racial groups in Canada;
4. Encourage and develop in persons of Chinese descent, a desire to know and to respect their historical and cultural heritage; to educate them in adopting a creative and positive attitude towards the Chinese Canadian contribution to society; 
5. Develop community resources through voluntary participation, community networks and coalition building; and 
6. Educate, train and empower Chinese Canadians in civic participation, social and political advocacy through participant-led programs.

The mission of the Jennifer Ashleigh Children's Charity is to improve the quality of life for seriously ill children and their families… "when love is not enough."

Norm Clements established this Charity in 1990 in memory of his granddaughter, Jennifer Ashleigh Clements who died at age six months from a degenerative, muscular disease. Her younger sister, Danica, died in infancy of the same illness just two years later.

The Jennifer Ashleigh Children's Charity assists children who are:
 - seriously ill;
 - have a permanent disability;
 - 18 years of age or under;
 - permanent residents of Ontario or Landed Immigrant status

Our charity acts as a financial safety net, helping families when all other resources have run out.

